MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found while auditing the Tribes page: QuestionCard's Edit/Delete
buttons never appeared for anyone, even a question's own author,
because community-new.tsx never passed currentUserId — the prop
isAuthor is computed from. Even if they had appeared, the handlers
were console.log stubs; PATCH/DELETE /api/questions/:id already
existed and worked, nothing on the client ever called them.

- Extended AskQuestionDialog with an optional edit mode (questionId +
  initialValues + externally-controlled open state) so the same form
  handles both creating and editing, using PATCH instead of POST when
  editing. Kept the existing create-mode call sites unchanged.
- community-new.tsx: pass currentUserId to QuestionCard, wire
  handleEditQuestion to open the dialog pre-filled with the question's
  data, wire handleDeleteQuestion to a real mutation against the
  existing DELETE endpoint, and render one controlled edit-dialog
  instance for the whole list rather than one per card.
- Recolored the stats row, search focus ring, and sort-tab active
  state from raw purple/pink/red to brand/accent tokens.
- Removed CommunityStats.tsx and StickyFilters.tsx — both imported
  into this page but never actually rendered, and not used anywhere
  else in the codebase.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
