The previous commit's message described wiring up question
Edit/Delete, but a git add ordering mistake meant only the two dead
file deletions were actually staged — the real code changes to
AskQuestionDialog.tsx and community-new.tsx never made it in. This
commit is those changes:

- AskQuestionDialog gets an optional edit mode (questionId +
  initialValues + externally-controlled open state), using PATCH
  instead of POST when editing.
- community-new.tsx passes currentUserId to QuestionCard (without
  it, isAuthor was always false and Edit/Delete never appeared for
  anyone), wires handleEditQuestion to open the dialog pre-filled,
  wires handleDeleteQuestion to a real DELETE mutation, and renders
  one controlled edit-dialog instance for the question list.
- Recolored the stats row, search focus ring, and sort-tab active
  state from raw purple/pink/red to brand/accent tokens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
